      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The experiments on cats under the conditions of acute myocardial ischemia showed that malate (20 and 100 mg/kg) and NAD (0.2 and 2 mg/kg) are able of increasing the coronary blood flow against the background of insignificantly increased oxygen consumption by the heart. The combination of these drugs (malate 100 mg/kg + NAD 0.2 mg/kg) produces an increase in the coronary blood flow and a dramatic raise in cardiac oxygen consumption."},
